# Client rules — UI, themes, render, audio

## Design tokens — no literals

**No component may contain a literal colour, font, radius, shadow or duration.** Everything reads
from the `--gol-*` custom-property contract in `src/themes/tokens.css`. A lint rule enforces this
from Phase 1. Token names must be theme-neutral (never `--gol-neon-pink`).

This is what lets six themes exist without six copies of the UI.

## Everything is a command

If a user can do it, it is a registered `AppCommand` with a title, a category and a keybinding (or
an explicit `noBinding: true`). A button's handler is `bus.run('sim.toggleRun')` and nothing else.

A test enumerates every command and fails on orphans. This discipline is why the Phase 4 command
palette is a *view* over an existing registry rather than a retrofit — if a feature is missing from
the palette, the bug is that the feature bypassed the registry.

## Rendering (ADR-005)

- One `Renderer` interface; Canvas2D through Phase 4, WebGL2 added in Phase 5. **No UI, theme or
  engine code may depend on which renderer is active.**
- Dirty-rect invalidation always. Never full-repaint when a rect will do; batch draws by colour;
  use the tile atlas below `cellSize` 4 and the density LOD below 1.
- Correct `devicePixelRatio` handling. Never render blurry.
- **The overlay layer (selection, cursor, grid lines, ghosts) is never obscured, tinted or blurred
  by a theme effect.** Usability outranks beauty.

## Themes are sensory modules (ADR-008)

Tokens + cell palette (with an age ramp) + render hooks + motion signature + sound pack.
A theme is finished only when a screenshot with the UI chrome cropped out is instantly
identifiable as that theme. If you can only tell by the button colours, it is not done.

Every theme declares a `cost`; the degrade governor measures real frame time and drops
post-process, then effects, then background — **visibly, never silently**. Quality 0 must hold
60 fps under 4× CPU throttling in every theme.

## Audio

**Zero audio assets** — everything is synthesised from WebAudio oscillators and noise buffers.
Muted by default, unlocked only by a user gesture, hard cap of 24 voices with oldest-first
stealing, look-ahead scheduling (25 ms tick / 100 ms horizon). High-rate events are **aggregated**,
never machine-gunned: at 10,000 births/sec the output is a texture, not 10,000 blips.

## Accessibility — a gate, not a nicety

- Every control keyboard-reachable with a visible focus ring; every icon-only control has an
  accessible name.
- WCAG AA contrast for chrome text **in every theme**; palettes distinguishable under
  deuteranopia and protanopia.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables non-essential animation, collapses every choreography
  to an instant state change, and silences ambient audio — with no exceptions.
- axe-core: zero violations, every panel, every theme.

## Feel

Optimistic painting — the cell lights up under the cursor before the worker confirms. Readouts
throttle to 10 Hz with tabular figures so nothing jitters. Every transition goes through the
theme's motion system, never a hardcoded CSS transition.
